{"category":"IndexError","root_cause":"The loop iterates over `words` from index 0 to the length of `words`, but when `word` equals `token`, the loop attempts to access `words[i + 1]`. If `i` is equal to the length of `words` minus one, then `i + 1` will be out of bounds.","corrected_code":"def after_token(words, token):
    """Return the word after the first matching token, or None."""
    for i, word in enumerate(words):
        if word == token:
            return words[i + 1] if i < len(words) - 1 else None
    return None","explanation":"To fix this issue, we need to check if `i` is less than the length of `words` minus one before accessing `words[i + 1]`. This prevents an `IndexError` when `i` is the last element of the list."}

