{"category":"WrongResult","root_cause":"The slice operation `text[i:i+n]` does not include the last element when `i + n == len(text)`, which causes an IndexError.","corrected_code":"def blocks(text, n):
    """Return chunks of n characters, retaining a final short chunk; n is positive."""
    if len(text) % n != 0:
        text += '_'
    return [text[i:i+n] for i in range(0, len(text)-n+1, n)]","explanation":"To fix this issue, we need to ensure that the last chunk includes the remaining characters after the division. We add an underscore (`_`) at the end of the string if its length is not divisible by `n`. This way, the last chunk will always have the correct number of characters."}

{"category":"WrongResult","root_cause":"The function `tally` does not correctly handle multiple calls without resetting the dictionary.","corrected_code":"def tally(keys, counts=None):
